  "body": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/interaction.html#sequential-focus-navigation-starting-point defines the \"sequential focus navigation starting point\", which lets UAs start tab-focusing from an arbitrary point in the document, even if the starting point isn't focusable.  It doesn't currently require using this in any way, tho.\n\nIE and Firefox both set this to the target element whenever you do a fragment nav, such as clicking on a ToC link.  Chrome doesn't, which means clicking a ToC link and then pressing tab jumps you back to the top of the page where the first links in the document are.  This is user-hostile (particularly for those that primarily use keyboard navigation), and is worked around by some authors with JS hacks.\n\nThe spec should just require this behavior.\n",
